## 8. Compliance

| ID | Requirement | Testable Criterion |
|----|-------------|-------------------|
| CXC-LINE-C1 | Compute/transfer overlap | Double-buffer full-frame wall time < single-buffer sum and ≤ (Σ compute + one-band transfer); measured on-device |
| CXC-LINE-C2 | Buffer-reuse safety | A compute pass never writes a buffer with a transfer in flight (wait enforced); no tearing under stress |
| CXC-LINE-C3 | Overlap degradation | Second-buffer OOM falls back to single-buffer blocking transfer; frame still correct; logged, non-fatal |
| CXC-LINE-C4 | Mode selection | Driver with ≥2 scan-out FBs → full-fb pointer-swap; <2 → band; full-fb refused on incapable board |
| CXC-LINE-C5 | Mode transparency | A widget renders pixel-identically (within [CXC-R-C1]) under full-fb and band modes |
| CXC-LINE-C6 | Dirty-band skip | A rect redraw re-renders+transfers only intersecting bands; clean bands untouched (per-band transfer counter + pixel-diff) |
| CXC-LINE-C7 | No global clear | Partial present does not blank clean bands; clean regions byte-stable across the partial frame |
| CXC-LINE-C8 | Idle no-op | Empty damage set → zero bands transfer, < 5 ms/frame |
| CXC-LINE-C9 | Full-damage degradation | All-band damage degrades to the full overlap path at ≤ the render_frame baseline |
| CXC-LINE-C10 | Animation viability | One small animating region (≤3 bands) sustains ≥30 fps on the classic CYD |
| CXC-LINE-C11 | Timeout safety | wait_band_transfer times out and recovers; no wedge |
| CXC-LINE-C12 | Coexistence | Band DMA coexists with WiFi/MQTT; MQTT task not starved during transfer |
| CXC-LINE-C13 | Glass gate | On-device: a gauge/needle tween and a [CXC-BIND-STATES] transition are smooth — no tearing/stale-seam/flicker (verify.human) |
| CXC-LINE-C14 | No GPL code | No Slint source vendored; technique lifted from public docs only |

